These regress tests use a local and a remote machine.  On the remote
machine inetd provides services.  The local machine runs scapy to
navigate the remote TCP stack through the TCP state diagram.
For active connections a Perl client is started on the remote machine.

tcp_closing	FIN packets are retransmitted in CLOSING state
tcp_established	data packets are retransmitted in ESTABLISHED state
tcp_finwait	FIN retransmitted in FIN_WAIT_1 and goto FIN_WAIT_2 state
tcp_finwaitidle	FIN_WAIT_2 after close is dropped on idle timeout
tcp_keepalive	RST is sent in ESTABLISHED state after keepalive timeout
tcp_lastack	FIN packets are retransmitted in LAST_ACK state
tcp_reassfull	reassembly queue length is limited for out of order segments
tcp_sack	data before a selective ACK block is retransmitted
tcp_sackbad	bogus selective ACK block is ignored
tcp_sacksnd	SACK retransmit does not move snd_max beyond data
tcp_shutidle	FIN_WAIT_2 after shutdown and close is dropped on idle timeout
tcp_syncache	SYN+ACK packets are retransmitted by SYN cache
tcp_synfin	FIN retransmitted after SYN_SENT via SYN_RCVD to FIN_WAIT_1
tcp_synrcvd	SYN+ACK retransmitted in SYN_RCVD after SYN_SENT state
tcp_synsent	SYN packets are retransmitted in SYN_SENT state
